{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_epd5gafocpqfka24cno6v6xvuzea76cuteeagznh24qe6cfn6kca","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Summary:\n\n## Phase A — surface mapped (artifacts in crate root)\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` exports exactly `driver` and `main`; enumerated build configs. `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]`** → one feature combination (verified mechanically by the script, not assumed).\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 26 rows derived by grepping every statement of the 36-line C file. The C ignores both `scanf`'s and `printf`'s return values, so the whole error surface is \"`x` keeps its initial `0`\" + unchecked signed overflow. Rows 24–26 document *why* the null-pointer/enum/length boundaries are vacuous (no pointer, enum, or length exists) — asserted structurally so the claim can't rot.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 30 rows across both entry points (the low-level `driver` FFI export, not just `main`).\n\n## Structural work needed to test at all\n`CMakeLists.txt` builds an *executable*, and `Cargo.toml` had only a bin. I split the translation into `src/driver_impl.rs`, shared by `src/main.rs` (bin) and a new `src/lib.rs` cdylib exporting `#[no_mangle] driver` + `main`, so the two artifacts can't drift. Tests build both `.so`s on demand (gcc; nested cargo with a separate `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to dodge the build lock), load them with `libloading`, and call **only** exported symbols — each in a forked child with fd 0/1 redirected (required: the harness's parallel output otherwise pollutes captured stdout, and `main` consumes process-wide stdio state).\n\n## Two real divergences found and fixed (Rust side only)\n1. **Broken pipe** — C died with `SIGPIPE` (signal 13), Rust exited 0, because Rust's runtime installs `SIG_IGN` before `main`. `src/main.rs` now restores `SIG_DFL`.\n2. **Closed stdout** — `println!` would panic on `EBADF`; now `write!` with an ignored error, matching C's ignored `printf` return.\n\nTwo other failures were wrong expectations in my *tests*, corrected against the C ground truth (never the C).\n\n## Results\n- **60 tests** (`symbols` 3, `valid_paths` 27, `error_paths` 24, `binary_diff` 6), all passing, **0 warnings**, ~10 s.\n- `nm -D` symbol diff: **empty**; no non-libc undefined symbols; both exports `dlsym`-reachable.\n- Every `CONFIGS.md` row (~70 000 `driver` values incl. a 65 536-value strided sweep of the whole `int` domain; ~2 400 `main` inputs) and every `ERRORS.md` row passes; glibc `%d` quirks confirmed against C (saturation at `LONG_MAX`/`LONG_MIN` then truncation to `int`, `0x10`→`0`, sign-then-EOF, chunk-boundary cases).\n- Passing under all three feature invocations (`--no-default-features`, default, `--all-features`) via `./run_all_configs.sh`, from a clean build state, plus an extra 4 100-input out-of-band fuzz (full byte range, and release profile) with 0 differences.\n- Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (only the sanctioned `c_src/build/` output)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1158,"cache_read_input_tokens":154710,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1158,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c52ecede-b212-4bcc-9ef3-1815ba16c715","uuid":"98c9d76a-a0bb-44fa-a6ff-3ee98ff51efa","timestamp":"2026-08-18T12:17:13.059Z"}
